  "narrative": {
    "intro": "South Carolina has received $544M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The federal government awarded 579 contracts in the state, with an average award size of $940K. Obligations fell 94.6% year over year. The Department of Energy is the largest buying agency in the state, obligating $443M so far in FY2027 to date. Savannah River Nuclear Solutions LLC is the largest vendor in South Carolina, receiving $379M in obligations in the same period. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligations, with $381M. Historical annual obligations show much larger totals in prior years, including $10.7B in FY24 and $10.1B in FY26, compared with $544M in FY27 to date. The top buying agencies after the Department of Energy include the Department of Veterans Affairs at $65.9M and the Department of Agriculture at $12.5M. The leading industries beyond Facilities Support Services include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $48.3M and Couriers and Express Delivery Services at $25.9M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal spending in South Carolina right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy accounts for a large share of current obligations, obligating $443M in FY2027 to date. Savannah River Nuclear Solutions LLC received $379M, and Facilities Support Services accounted for $381M of obligations, indicating concentration in a few agencies, vendors, and industries. Historical annual totals were higher, for example $10.7B in FY24 and $10.1B in FY26, compared with $544M in FY27 to date. The top vendors and industries together show that a small set of buyers and contractors dominate current obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What should contractors know about the FY2027 to date market in South Carolina?",
        "body": "The market in FY2027 to date is smaller than recent full fiscal years, with total obligations of $544M and award count of 579. The average award size is $940K, and obligations are down 94.6% year over year. Major opportunities in this partial year appear with the Department of Energy at $443M and with large incumbent vendors such as Savannah River Nuclear Solutions LLC at $379M. Contractors in facilities support, R&D, and courier services match the leading industry areas by obligations."
      }
